# Styling

- Plain CSS files next to the component they style. No CSS frameworks. Do not add Tailwind-style utility classes (`p-6`, `bg-blue-600`) — nothing processes them.
- Theme tokens live in `src/styles/global.css` on `.light-mode` and `.dark-mode`, with `:root` fallbacks for the first paint: `--background-color`, `--text-color`, `--muted-color`, `--hover-color`, `--accent-color`, `--accent-contrast`, `--accent-soft`, `--surface-hover`, `--border-color`. Use `--surface-hover` for hover fills and `--border-color` for visible dividers; `--surface-hover` is too faint to read as a border.
- Use one accent. New highlights reuse `--accent-color` / `--accent-soft` rather than introducing another colour.
- A stylesheet only styles its own component's classes. Do not override another component's class from a parent stylesheet: CSS import order follows component import order, so a child's stylesheet loads last and silently wins, media query or not.
- The global `h1` is the home-page hero size. Routed pages (blog posts, heatmap) scope their own title down in that page's stylesheet. Do not shrink the global `h1` to fit a sub-page.
- The shell stacks at `max-width: 900px`. Both `app/App.css` and `shared/navigation/Sidebar.css` use that value; change them together, along with the sidebar's sticky `top`, which must match the `.app` top margin.
- On desktop, `.app` is a three-column grid (`1fr | 42rem | 1fr`) so the reading column is centred in the viewport. The sidebar sits in the left track. Pages without a sidebar (`blogPost`) still occupy the centre track. The commute heatmap spans the full grid because it is a map, not a document. Do not go back to a flex row that parks the document to the right of the sidebar.
- Keep vertical spacing in `rem`. A percentage margin or padding resolves against the container's **width**, so it grows with screen width.
- Vertical rhythm comes from the container's flex `gap`, not from stacked margins and padding. `.main-content` spaces top-level content; `.home-preview` spaces a preview's label, card, and link. Text elements (`p`, `h2`, `h3`) carry bottom margin only, and `p:last-child` drops it, so a leading heading or trailing paragraph never adds to the gap around its container.
- `.SubSection` pads for its hover background and cancels that padding with an equal negative margin. That keeps card text on the same left edge as content without a card. Change the padding and margin together.
- Homepage collection labels are restrained eyebrow headings, not large section titles. Full collection routes use `PageLayout` and a visible page title.
- Below 900px the primary navigation is hidden. Phones navigate through the homepage preview links and the labelled back links, so any new route must be reachable that way too, not only from the sidebar.
- Prefer flex or grid with `min-width: 0` over fixed offsets like `margin-left: 30rem`, so intermediate widths degrade instead of overlapping.
- Use `:focus-visible` with `outline` and `outline-offset`. Never use `border` for focus, which shifts layout.
- Responsive changes need coverage in `e2e/layout.spec.ts`, which runs on desktop and both phone viewports.
